course: dictionary
lesson: 8621
title: Scribe: the writer by hand
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A scribe was a person whose job was to write or copy documents by hand, before printing was invented. Read the words around the word to find out more. «Scribes pressed a cut reed into wet clay, making wedge-shaped marks.» Pressing marks into clay is a kind of writing, so a scribe is a writer.
explain: Scribe can also mean an adult who writes down a pupil's answers in a test. «If your writing arm is in a cast, school can help with a scribe (someone who writes for you).» The words in brackets give the meaning, so check your idea by swapping in «someone who writes for you». It still makes sense.
explain: In the Bible, the scribes were experts in Jewish law. In a funny, informal way, a scribe can also mean a writer or journalist. Think about the sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A scribe was a person who wrote or copied documents by hand, before printing.
fact: In Sumer about 4,000 years ago, boys trained as scribes in «tablet houses», copying signs again and again.
fact: Around 1820, only about one adult in eight could read, and scribes were among the few who could.
fact: Informally, a scribe can mean a writer or journalist, as a joke about someone who writes a lot.
exercise: «Scribes pressed a cut reed into wet clay, making wedge-shaped marks.» What was a scribe's job here? | *Writing or copying by hand | Growing reeds by a river | Digging clay out of the ground | Selling food in a market
exercise: «If your writing arm is in a cast, school can help with a scribe (someone who writes for you).» What does scribe mean here? | A teacher who marks your work | A fast kind of printer | *Someone who writes for you
exercise: «In Sumer, boys trained as scribes, copying signs again and again.» Find and copy one word that shows the boys practised over and over. | houses | Sumer | tablet | *again
test: «The Bible speaks of the scribes and Pharisees.» In the Bible, what were the scribes? | Painters of pictures | *Experts in Jewish law | Children who play outdoors | Ships that sail the sea
test: In a test, a scribe is who? | A book of test questions | A ruler for drawing lines | *An adult who writes down a pupil's answers | A pupil who finishes first
exam: A friend jokes, «Mum says I'm the family scribe, because I write every birthday card.» What does scribe mean here? | A shop that sells cards | A cook who makes birthday cakes | *A person who writes a lot, like a writer | A child who cannot write
